# Cork API key (Bearer token, generated in Cork's Admin UI -> Settings ->
# API). Cork's OpenAPI spec also documents an OAuth2 flow for their own
# remote MCP server, but the underlying credential is the same API key -
# this connector only ever holds a live bearer key.
CORK_API_KEY=

# HTTP transport only (MCP_TRANSPORT=http): REQUIRED. The server refuses to
# start with this empty or set to a placeholder (fail closed, CWE-306).
# Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
CONDUIT_S2S_SECRET=
# Local development only: allow HTTP without a secret. Skips X-Gateway-S2S and
# binds 127.0.0.1 only. Never set in a deployed environment.
# MCP_ALLOW_INSECURE_DEV=1
